SUMMARY:Layer The Walls: Turn of the Century
DESCRIPTION:Saturday\, November 21\, 2026 • 3 PM • Steinman Hall What i
 f the walls of a home could tell the stories of everyone who lived there? 
 In one New York City tenement\, forty layers of wallpaper hold traces of t
 he immigrant families who made it their home. Behind each layer is a story
  of courage\, survival\, and the search for a better life Through imaginat
 ive puppetry\, masks\, and live performance\, Layer the Walls brings these
  remarkable stories to life—from an Irish immigrant helping build the Br
 ooklyn Bridge to Italian brothers caught in the Great Blizzard of 1888 and
  Russian Jewish garment workers who stood together to demand safer working
  conditions. Moving\, inventive\, and deeply human\, Layer the Walls is a 
 story about the people who came before us\, and the stories worth remember
 ing. Tickets: Adults $15 | Students $10 Recommended for ages 8 Make an aft
 ernoon of it! Free kids’ activities and crafts begin in the lobby at 2 P
 M ASL interpretation\, audio description\, sensory-friendly accommodations
 \, and a pre-show touch tour will be available. Interested? Contact Barry 
